  "interpretation": [
    "The video-only RTL model reproduces the hardware selection-gap durations and ordinals, total display counter and associated timestamp count; no audio, host scheduling or HDMI scaler model is needed for this reproduction.",
    "Hardware telemetry alone still does not encode unique picture identity. The eleven skipped and two repeated picture counts are proven in simulation; the matching net total is supporting hardware evidence, not a unique-picture hardware capture.",
    "Reference admission during B drain accepts a following reference without retaining capacity. Completion/header timing also loses release information. Full traces show ignored or overwritten pending references.",
    "A B header can precede its I reference completion by one decoder clock. The scheduler binds a previously displayed P and ignores the actual I completion; the metadata owner has already changed current_is_b and drops the retiring I descriptor.",
    "Published pictures also expose seventeen stale TFF/RFF descriptors and one lost initial PTS-valid flag. Fixing only the display counter or admitting the right bank would be insufficient.",
    "All twenty-five helper timestamps agree with authored field cadence within 2.5 ticks (27.8 microseconds). This helper stream has no large final timestamp hold to excuse the measured pauses; earlier remarks about a terminal timestamp gap must not be applied to this transport without evidence.",
    "The DDR cases are sensitivity tests, not measured device timing. Additional audio coupling is not excluded and must be checked after correcting video ownership and cadence."
  ],
  "proposed_fix_pending_approval": "Make reference retirement and following-header admission explicit across the scheduler and timestamp owner. Preserve the retiring picture identity, PTS and TFF/RFF/progressive descriptor; keep a following P/I payload blocked when its reference slot is occupied; bind early B headers to the reference actually completing, not an older promotion. Require both reduced tests to pass and all 289 pictures to publish once in display order with exact descriptors/PTS and authored film cadence in the integrated ideal/contended runs. Preserve paired pixel bounds, then propose a clean timing-audited FPGA build and original audio hardware retest. Do not change clocks, seeds or buffer sizes speculatively.",
